Subject: ntdll: name the real reason not to use the ASLR switch, and finish the trace fixes

The "this is not a fix" list in 0028 was missing the sharpest entry, and it is
not about wasted address space. The server-assigned base is what makes every
process in the prefix agree on where a DLL lives, and sections marked
IMAGE_SCN_MEM_SHARED|MEM_WRITE are mapped MAP_SHARED from shared_file
(map_image_into_view). With per-process bases, relocations one process applies
inside such a section are visible to the others, pointing at addresses that are
wrong there -- cross-process memory corruption, not merely fragmentation. Given
the comment exists to stop someone reaching for the switch, that belongs in it.

Two smaller ones from the same review:

  - The vprot cap banner was written before the record that filled the cap, so
    the log read "later calls are NOT recorded" and then showed one more. It now
    follows the record and marks the true end.
  - The empty-string debugstr_loadorder fix reached only the forced branch. The
    environment branch one line above still printed it raw, so
    WINEDLLOVERRIDES="foo=" traced as "got environment  for ..." -- no verdict
    token, in exactly the A/B that most needs to be readable.

Found in review.

